      "reported_material_gaps": [],
      "research_rationale": "The complete original page confirms one designation covering thirteen agencies under EO 7916 section 6. The complete EO 9830 and official pages 1, 3, 4 and 11 confirm express whole-order revocation effective May 1, 1947 and no target-specific saving. Primary EO 7916 pages 8\u20139 show a February 1, 1939 implementation bound followed by continuing director duties, so initial establishment does not exhaust the designation. Actual EO 8044 limits competitive coverage; actual EO 8363 changes parent section 3 and EO 8467 changes section 7. None changes section 6 or names EO 7975-A. Wrong adjacent instrument attributions in the prior review were corrected from original pages. No earlier end was found in the stated bounded searches and primary checks. Exact sources and limitations appear in ANALYSIS.md and SUPPLEMENT_RECEIPT.json.\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"The complete primary EO 7916, PDF pages 8\u20139, printed pages 1526\u20131527, makes establishment effective not later than February 1, 1939 and assigns continuing liaison, budget, supervision, training, grievance and Council duties. That implementation bound is not a sunset; no actual completion date is inferred. Actual EO 8043 amends Schedules A/B. Actual EO 8044 suspends only the competitive-coverage function. Actual EO 8363, rather than neighboring 8364, modifies parent section 3. Actual EO 8467, rather than neighboring 8468, restates section 7 effective July 1, 1940 while retaining personnel directors as ex officio Council members. Relevant complete personnel provisions and original pages were read. No earlier first end was found within the disclosed bounds. The owner unnamed-instrument and amendment rulings were applied without inventing dates for unproved reorganizations.\",\"independent_command_check\":\"The original contains one uniform designation and compliance requirement covering thirteen agencies. It contains no independent report, payment, return or other implementation clause. Primary parent section 6 imports continuing director liaison, budget, supervision, training and grievance duties; creating a division does not exhaust these functions. The whole designation and its imported obligations are reached by the same express revocation. No actual occurrence is inferred.\",\"savings_check\":\"The original contains no savings. The complete EO 9830 has no reservation of the target designation. Section 01.3 independently requires personnel offices; section 01.5 expressly continues and renames the Council of Personnel Administration. That separate institutional continuation is disclosed, rather than treated as continuation of the revoked thirteen-agency designation. No target-specific accrued or transferred right was found in these complete texts.\",\"scope_check\":\"The sole operative paragraph, original characters 776:1682, designates thirteen agencies under one parent provision. Original PDF page 1 was visually checked, confirming the list, number, date and complete operative boundary. EO 9830 Part III names EO 7975-A in full without a target-specific limitation; its global May 1 effective date applies to all thirteen objects. No inventory correction is proposed.\"}",
